  {
   "id": "18104178755183321",
   "date": "2026-08-06",
   "caption": "This one's for sale.\n72 x 40, built from heart fir joists out of Brown's Pottery in Arden, North Carolina. That building went up around 1940 and the Browns made pottery in it until 2019 \u2014 the family has been working clay in this country since the 1700s. When the place was gutted the framing got pulled and sold instead of landfilled, and it reached me through a lumber dealer in Brevard.\nI planed the joists down and made them a table. The black marks in the top are the original nail holes. Finish is Rubio Monocoat Oil Plus 2C in Pure \u2014 no stain on it. That color is eighty years of being a building.\nWhoever takes it home gets a plaque with their family name on it.\nDM me for the price.",
